  "id": "Compound::DB00169 - Gene::7421",
  "verbalization": "Cholecalciferol, a form of vitamin D, is consistently linked to Vdr through multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that Cholecalciferol, through its structural similarities to dihydrotachysterol and calcidiol, binds to Vdr, a key component of the vitamin D receptor. This binding is supported by multiple paths, with Cholecalciferol being a direct target of Vdr in several cases. The presence of secondary alcohol and hydroxy seco-steroid intermediates further underscores the biochemical relationship between these entities. The integration of these pathways highlights a mechanistic link between Cholecalciferol and Vdr, where the structural similarities and functional interactions are central to the observed effects. The evidence is robust and consistent, reinforcing the role of Vdr in the biological response to Cholecalciferol.",
